      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Volvulus of the mobile spleen is a rare condition generally manifested by acute sudden onset abdominal pain localized in the left flank. Ultrasound or computed tomographic imaging generally provides the diagnosis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE REPORT",
          "content": "An 18-year-old patient was hospitalized for acute pain of the left flank that had begun 48 hours earlier. The abdominal scan visualized a volvulus of a mobile spleen. Laparoscopic distortion was successful, allowing normal recoloration of the spleen."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION",
          "content": "Rapid intervention is crucial for conservative treatment. Laparoscopic treatment allows distortion manoeuvres and splenopexia using a mesh. This is the first reported case of successful conservative laparoscopic treatment of volvulus of a mobile spleen."
        }
      ]},
